#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
In the book, remove the two experimental pages that are vaguely ascii versions of the cover we've been working on, don't remove the big comment at the top that's got similar stuff, and revert the source key and font key pages to a few versions ago of them before we started messing with the font size. Then look in the cover directory and find the -5- files, those are two more accurate representation of the spacing on the cover. Read the 'up' file, and try to JUST adjust the fine grained positioning of letters in the 'dn' file to make the 'dn' file more well-aligned like the 'up' file is. Don't make any big changes. Just make dn more polished like up.
EOF
